   "`ptr` can be `*T`, `?*T`, or `[]T`. Changes the alignment of a pointer. The alignment to use is inferred based on the result type.\n\nA [pointer alignment safety check](https://ziglang.org/documentation/0.16.0/#Incorrect-Pointer-Alignment) is added to the generated code to make sure the pointer is aligned as promised.",
   :documentation-format :markdown,
   :documentation-source :zls-langref,
   :eval-to-error :never,
   :illegal-outside-function? false,
