   "Returns the smallest integral value not less than the given floating point number. Uses a dedicated hardware instruction when available.\n\nSupports [Floats](https://ziglang.org/documentation/0.16.0/#Floats) and [Vectors](https://ziglang.org/documentation/0.16.0/#Vectors) of floats.\n\nWhen the inferred result type is an [integer](https://ziglang.org/documentation/0.16.0/#Integers), the integer part is extracted from the ceiled result. If that value cannot fit in the destination type, it invokes safety-checked [Illegal Behavior](https://ziglang.org/documentation/0.16.0/#Illegal-Behavior).",
